    <string name="ob_ack">I understand Retfast is not an emergency service and that I must call 112 / normal emergency channels in an emergency.</string>
    <string name="ob1_title">What is Retfast?</string>
    <string name="ob1_body">Retfast is live flight tracking and landed-pilot retrieval for paragliding events. You apply to an event, the organizer assigns your role, your flight shows on the event map and after landing you can request a retrieve.</string>
    <string name="ob2_title">Roles</string>
    <string name="ob2_body">Roles are per event: pilots fly and request retrieves, retrievers pick landed pilots up by car, observers watch the map, organizers manage applications. You do not choose a role when applying; the organizer picks it on approval.</string>
    <string name="ob3_title">How tracking works</string>
    <string name="ob3_body">When you start a flight Retfast stores GPS positions on the phone and shares them with the event. While recording you see a permanent \'Retfast is recording your flight\' notification — Android requires it for background work. Recording continues with the screen locked.</string>
    <string name="ob4_title">Retrieve</string>
    <string name="ob4_body">After landing you send a retrieve request. It is saved on the phone first and delivered when you have signal. When a retriever accepts you see their name, phone and position; steps are ticked only when the server confirms them.</string>
    <string name="ob5_title">Background location and battery</string>
    <string name="ob5_body">For reliable recording grant location \'Allow all the time\' (Android asks on a separate screen). We recommend exempting Retfast from battery optimisation; some manufacturers (Xiaomi, Huawei, Samsung, Oppo…) kill apps aggressively. Swiping the app from recents usually does not stop the service, but \'Force stop\' ends recording for good — do not do it during a flight.</string>
    <string name="ob6_title">Connectivity and GPS limits</string>
    <string name="ob6_body">Cellular coverage in valleys and mountains drops often. Recording continues offline and points are sent when signal returns, so the live map can lag. GPS altitude is not barometric and vertical speed is only an estimate.</string>
    <string name="ob7_title">Not an emergency service</string>
    <string name="ob7_body">Retfast is a logistics and tracking tool, not a rescue or emergency-help service. In case of injury or danger call 112 and use normal emergency channels. The app never calls rescue services automatically.</string>
    <string name="permissions_title">Permissions</string>
    <string name="permissions_sub">Four steps for reliable background recording. Each is optional but best done in order.</string>
    <string name="perm_fine_title">Precise location</string>
    <string name="perm_fine_body">GPS position is needed for recording and retrieves. Choose \'Precise\', not \'Approximate\'.</string>
    <string name="perm_coarse_only">Only approximate location is granted. Allow precise location.</string>
    <string name="perm_allow">Allow</string>
    <string name="perm_bg_title">Background location (\'All the time\')</string>
    <string name="perm_bg_body">Needed so recording continues with the screen locked or another app open.</string>
    <string name="perm_bg_honest">Android asks for this on a system settings screen, not in the app: choose \'Allow all the time\'. It is only used while you record a flight, wait for a retrieve or are on retriever duty.</string>
    <string name="perm_bg_open">Ask for \'all the time\'</string>
    <string name="perm_notif_title">Notifications</string>
    <string name="perm_notif_body">For the recording notification and the \'Did you land?\' reminder. If denied, recording still works but you will not see the notification.</string>
    <string name="perm_battery_title">Battery optimisation</string>
    <string name="perm_battery_body">Exempting Retfast reduces the chance Android puts recording to sleep. Not mandatory.</string>
    <string name="perm_battery_ask">Ask for exemption</string>
    <string name="perm_battery_oem">On some manufacturers you must also enable \'Autostart\' or \'Allow background activity\' (Settings &gt; Battery / Apps).</string>
